# Google Sign-In (api/auth.js 'google' action) + Google Calendar Sync (api/calendar.js).
# Same OAuth client for both -- create it in Google Cloud Console (OAuth client ID, Web
# application type), enable the Google Calendar API for the project, and add this app's
# real domain(s) as Authorized JavaScript origins. GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET is only needed for
# Calendar Sync's incremental-auth code exchange (api/calendar.js?action=connect) -- Sign-
# In alone (an ID token, not an auth code) never needs it. Also set GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID as the
# literal value of the frontend's GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID constant (ptw-pwa-v2.html, near
# initGoogleSignIn) once issued -- that one intentionally isn't an env var since it ships
# to the browser either way.
GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=
